IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssaa-types`

-- Social Security Administration Act 1992 (UK) — GOALS 1-3: RECOVERABLE
-- OVERPAYMENTS, OFFENCES, AND THE PENALTY AS AN ALTERNATIVE TO PROSECUTION.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1992-5.txt.

§ `Goal 1 — recoverable overpayments (s 71)`

-- s 71(1) "Where it is determined that, whether fraudulently or otherwise,
-- any person has misrepresented, or failed to disclose, any material fact and
-- in consequence ... a payment has been made ..., the Secretary of State
-- shall be entitled to recover the amount of any payment which he would not
-- have made". (5A): not unless the determination under which it was paid
-- has been reversed on appeal, revised or superseded.
@ref s 71(1), (3), (5A)
@export The amount recoverable from a person under s 71 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 (UK): the amount overpaid in consequence of their misrepresentation or failure to disclose a material fact (fraudulent or not), once the awarding decision has been revised, superseded or reversed on appeal; otherwise 0. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS AN `Overpayment facts`  @desc The misrepresentation or non-disclosure, causation, the revision of the decision, and the amount
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount recoverable under s 71 for` o MEANS
    IF       o's `misrepresented or failed to disclose a material fact`
         AND o's `payment made in consequence`
         AND o's `awarding decision revised, superseded or reversed`
    THEN o's `amount overpaid`
    ELSE 0

§ `Goal 2 — offences (ss 111A, 112)`

DECLARE `Benefit offence` IS ONE OF
    `no offence`
    `an offence under s 111A (dishonesty)`
    `an offence under s 112`

-- s 111A(1)-(1B): the conduct done "dishonestly" ((4): "knowingly" in
-- Scotland). s 112(1)-(1B): the same conduct with knowledge, without
-- dishonesty. Where both are made out, s 111A is the more serious.
@ref ss 111A(1)-(1B), (4), 112(1)-(1B)
@export Which offence, if any, is committed under ss 111A or 112 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 (UK): s 111A where the false statement or failure to notify is dishonest (in Scotland, done knowingly); otherwise s 112 where its knowledge and other elements are met. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN f IS AN `Offence facts`  @desc The conduct, whether its elements are met, dishonesty, and Scotland
GIVETH A `Benefit offence`
`the benefit offence for` f MEANS
    IF   NOT (f's `the knowledge and other elements are met`)
    THEN `no offence`
    ELSE IF   f's `dishonestly` OR f's `in Scotland`
         THEN `an offence under s 111A (dishonesty)`
         ELSE `an offence under s 112`

DECLARE `Maximum sentence` HAS
    `summary, months`                                   IS A NUMBER
    -- NOTHING: summary only.
    `on indictment, years`                              IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- s 111A(3): six months summary; seven years on indictment. s 112(2): summary
-- only, three months.
@ref ss 111A(3), 112(2)
GIVEN o IS A `Benefit offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Maximum sentence`
`the maximum sentence for` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `no offence` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an offence under s 111A (dishonesty)` THEN JUST (`Maximum sentence` OF 6, JUST 7)
    WHEN `an offence under s 112` THEN JUST (`Maximum sentence` OF 3, NOTHING)

§ `Goal 3 — penalty as an alternative to prosecution (s 115A)`

-- s 115A(1): a recoverable overpayment attributable to the person's act or
-- omission, with grounds for proceedings; (1A): no overpayment, but grounds
-- for proceedings and an overpayment would have been recoverable.
@ref s 115A(1), (1A), (2)
GIVEN p IS A `Penalty facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a penalty notice may be given for` p IF
        p's `grounds for proceedings for an offence`
    AND p's `the overpayment would be recoverable`
    AND ((NOT (p's `an overpayment was made`)) OR p's `attributable to the person's act or omission`)

-- s 115A(3) "50% of the amount of the overpayment (rounded down to the
-- nearest whole penny), subject to— (a) a minimum amount of £350, and (b) a
-- maximum amount of £5000." (3A): £350 in a (1A) case.
@ref s 115A(3)-(3A)
@export The administrative penalty under s 115A of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 (UK): 50% of the overpayment rounded down to the penny, at least £350 and at most £5,000; £350 where no overpayment was made (s 115A(1A)); 0 where no penalty notice may be given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Penalty facts`  @desc Whether an overpayment was made and its amount, and the conditions for a notice
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the administrative penalty for` p MEANS
    IF   NOT (`a penalty notice may be given for` p)
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF   NOT (p's `an overpayment was made`)
         THEN 350
         ELSE BRANCH
                IF half LESS THAN 350 THEN 350
                IF half GREATER THAN 5000 THEN 5000
                OTHERWISE half
    WHERE
        half MEANS FLOOR (p's `amount overpaid` TIMES 50) DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 115A(5): agreement may be withdrawn "at any time during the period of 14
-- days beginning with the day on which he agrees to pay it".
@ref s 115A(5)
@export The last day to withdraw agreement to pay an administrative penalty under s 115A(5) of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 (UK): the end of the 14 days beginning with the day of agreement (that day + 13); NOTHING if there was no agreement. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Penalty facts`  @desc The day the person agreed to pay
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to withdraw agreement for` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `agreed to pay on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d  THEN JUST (Date (Day d PLUS 13))
